A column goes on purpose, and a view still reads it. SQLite would make the
view and fail at the request that reads it; roux-db reads every view of
schema.sql, so the build says it.

== before
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL, note TEXT) STRICT;
CREATE VIEW notes AS SELECT id, note FROM dish;
INSERT INTO dish VALUES (1, 'soup', 'hot');

== after
-- @release 1
-- @drop 1 column dish note
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;
CREATE VIEW notes AS SELECT id, note FROM dish;

== error
roux-db: view notes: no such column: note
